\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Higher Late In Line With Rupiah's Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 222 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 1997\par 10:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is higher against the U.S. dollar in late trading Monday, after concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize the Indonesian rupiah also boosted \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0945 GMT (4:45 a.m. EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.5565, down from S$1.5730 at Monday's open and S$1.5845 in late Asian trading on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's rise Monday shadowed that of the rupiah, which strengthened by around 9% after the central banks of Indonesia, Singapore and Japan acted in unison to buy an estimated $500 billion worth of rupiah. \par \par \uc2  In the local money markets, short-term interest rates continue to ease following the liquidity squeeze of recent weeks. The overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is currently quoted at 2.50%-2.625%, down from 3.75%-3.875% earlier and 4.25%-4.5% in late trading Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At the same time, the three-month interbank has dropped to\par 4.00%-4.125% from 4.50%-5.00% earlier. Late Friday, the three-month rate\par was quoted at 4.25%-4.5%.\par -Tom Holland; 65 421 4800; tom.holland@djmarkets.com.sg\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-11-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0951GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtb308ciz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
