\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  MAS Says  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Mkt 'On Its Own Account' \b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 1997\par 09:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore said Monday it acted 'on its own account' in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to buy rupiah against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  In response to queries from Dow Jones, the authority, which is the country's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also said it bought rupiah against the U.S. dollar on behalf of the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  Over the weekend, the The International Monetary Fund announced a US$38 billion economic package for Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  However, President Suharto said last week that Singapore has agreed to extend U.S.$5 billion to buy rupiah and another U.S.$5 billion to supplement Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  As reported earlier Monday, Singapore's Finance Ministry said central banks of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japan and Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy rupiah against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  It said the depreciation of the rupiah in recent months has been excessive and the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflected confidence in the macroeconomic policies of the Indonesian government. \par \par \uc2  -By Joseph Rajendran; (65) 323 6656 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0817GMT \par \par \uc2