\par\par \b \uc2  Japan's MOF confirms  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 3 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday confirmed that the Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in concert with Indonesian and Singaporean monetary authorities to defend the Indonesian rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "Three authorities agreed that they would be ready to act in the market as and when necessary in the future," a statement by Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said. \par \par \uc2  "This \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aimed at correcting excessive depreciation of the Indonesian rupiah," Mitsuzuka said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  "I firmly believe that it should, together with the agreement of the Indonesian package formulated by the IMF, World Bank and Asian Development Bank, contribute to stabilising the Indonesian economy," he said. \par \par \uc2  In a separate statement, the Bank of Japan said it bought rupiah for dollars in the market. It did not specify the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged on news of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as the announcement of widespread economic reforms in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb303ebs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
