\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging market  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  - global snapshot. \b0\par\par\uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 31 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed on Friday as the dust began to settle on global markets, though most units looked set to complete the week well off troughs set during the turmoil. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's financial rescue package, organised by the International Monetary Fund, stole the limelight in Asia. While the rupiah held firm after the announcement, Jakarta stocks reacted negatively. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the full extent of the international package was yet to be made public, but it now looked likely to exceed $20 billion. \par \par \uc2  "It's pretty clear now this is going to be a massive package," said Carlos Daurignac, emerging markets strategist at Credit Agricole Indosuez. "The danger, however is we get a buy-the-rumour/sell-the-fact reaction from the rupiah and the stock market reaction was worrying in this respect." \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Thai baht continued to spiral lower to record lows, but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to stabilise the South Korean won. \par \par \uc2  In central Europe, the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the market by surprise and raised its key interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The crown was a touch softer against the mark after the hike, but analysts welcomed the move as a pro-active step. It showed the authorities were not willing to depend on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves alone to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The following is a brief snapshot of a selected group of emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves overnight. \par \par \uc2  ASIA \par \par \uc2  * Indonesian rupiah firms 1.0 percent against the dollar from Thursday, although still slightly weaker from last Friday. Market concerned about negative stock reaction to IMF package and there are jitters about durability of a wave of new carry trades put on the rupiah in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  * Final details of IMF package still awaited, but reports show IMF committing $10 billion and Asian Development Bank $3.5 billion. With bilateral deals from Singapore, Malaysia, Japan and Australia, whole package could exceed $20 billion. \par \par \uc2  * Onshore Thai baht spirals lower, down 2.8 percent from Thursday, but off new record low set at 41.97 per dollar. Investors fret about unstable political situation. Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it has net foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  commitments of $23.9 billion. \par \par \uc2  * South Korean won stabilises, little changed from Thursday and off record low of 984.70 set yesterday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars. \par \par \uc2  * Malaysian ringgit and \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar both a touch firmer, while Philippine peso and Indian Rupee slightly softer from Thursday. New Taiwanese dollar little changed \par \par \uc2  EASTERN EUROPE \par \par \uc2  * Czech crown a little weaker versus mark despite surprise Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate hike, pushing two-week repo rate to 14.8 percent versus 14.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  * Volatile Polish zloty hovering about 2.32/2.35 percent versus \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket compared with minus 2.12/2.91 percent at the open. Zloty little changed at 3.5000/5200 per dollar, but slightly firmer at 2.0245/10 per mark from Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  * Hungarian forint opens unchanged versus basket at 1.90 percent above parity, slightly firmer versus mark at 112.83. \par \par \uc2  * Slovak crown softer at 0.3 below parity versus target basket compared with 0.02 percent on Thursday. Little changed versus mark \par \par \uc2  * Russian rouble firmer versus dollar from Thursday at 5900/5905 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said rouble liquidity on interbank market fell sharply on Friday as speculative hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand dried up. \par \par \uc2  LATIN AMERICA \par \par \uc2  * Mexican peso rises 3.1 percent from Thursday's close amid easing in global market turbulence \par \par \uc2  * Brazilian real firmer at 1.1015/40 per dollar after speculative pressure Thursday forced \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to almost double its key monthly interest rate to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Government aide said $4-$5 billion spent on defending real this week. \par \par \uc2  AFRICA \par \par \uc2  * South Africa's rand firmer at 4.8150, local dealers cite profit-taking on short rand positions \par \par \uc2  * Kenyan shilling little changed at 63.80 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  --Mike Dolan, London newsroom +44 171 542 6762 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtav03ew5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
