\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -3: Mkt Nervous Of More Stk Mkt Falls \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1997\par 13:05\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The only exception was the Singapore dollar, which\par finished Asian trading at S$1.5785 to the U.S. dollar,\par stronger than S$1.5810 at Monday's close. Although it too\par weakened sharply in early trading, the slide was halted by\par what many traders believed was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the republic's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which\par was thought to have bought Singapore dollars to support the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    As the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rebounded, the MAS was again\par detected in the market, this time selling Singapore dollars\par to nudge the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  back down again.\par    "The MAS has just been trying to smooth out the market\par and reduce the volatility," said the U.S. bank's trading\par chief.\par    But Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to weaken\par further, regardless of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action, if global stock\par markets continue to fall, say many observers.\par    "Everything now hinges on the stock markets," says Fred\par Wu, head of economic research at the Development Bank of\par Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "If these falls continue, we will see a large\par reallocation of assets to highly-rated, liquid fixed-income\par instruments denominated in safe haven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - U.S.\par Treasury bonds and German Bunds," he said, arguing that such\par a reallocation of investment capital could knock 2\par percentage points off Singapore's 1998 GDP growth, reducing\par it to 3.5%-4% from an initial forecast of 5.5%-6%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS  10-28-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0705EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtas02ahq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
