\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand woes send new SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  shockwaves. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Angela Tan \par \uc2 883 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Oct 21 (Reuters) - Southeast Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under renewed selling on Tuesday after mounting political unrest in Thailand, and dealers said they saw no immediate reprieve for regionals yet. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone is buying dollars. They see more downside for most regionals and there is more pain to come," said a dealer with a U.S. institution. \par \par \uc2  Bears took the reigns again on renewed political uncertainties in Thailand after the resignation of its Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya on Monday sparked street protests calling for Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh to step down. \par \par \uc2  "The anti-Chavalit protests and demostrations are coming at a bad time when the country is trying to regain investors' confidence. Any resignation is going to send the baht tumbling and regionals as well, due to the close links Southeast Asia has," said another dealer with a U.S. institution. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht sank to a record low of 38.40 to the dollar in the onshore market as investors offloaded the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was quoted at 38.500/650 at 0955 GMT. \par \par \uc2  In the offshore market, the baht was at 38.650/750. \par \par \uc2  "I think people are just panicking now. They are just buying at any price. I think we should stop around 39 but it is uncharted territory," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah's upside was capped by the gloom spreading from Thailand. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 3,630.00/0.00 against the dollar, a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased rules to improve liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah was mixed as some offshore players absorbed the news by selling dollars, while others interpreted it as a chance for further rupiah weakening. \par \par \uc2  "It's quite a mixed picture. But it creates a two-way market. We see some offshores are cashing out from dollars on anticipation of increased supply due to a cut in the reserve rate," one U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But others look at the danger of increased rupiah supply which could trigger increased hedging activities. I don't know which factor is going to emerge stronger," he added. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia on Monday reopened its short-term securities (SBPUs) facility and cut \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve requirements for banks to three from five percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah was capped by the potential outcome of negotiations with an International Monetary Fund (IMF)-led team for an economic aid package. \par \par \uc2  IMF Managing Director Michel Camdessus said on Monday in France that IMF talks with Indonesia were extremely constructive and he hoped for an important deal soon. \par \par \uc2  A bearish cloud continued to hover over the Malaysian ringgit, with dealers expecting it to test 3.4000 to a dollar in the next one to two weeks. \par \par \uc2  "There is still more downside room for the ringgit. The post-budget excitement is over and regional gloom, led by Thailand, has taken over again," said the dealer with a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0955 GMT, the ringgit was at 3.3340/9 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  A survey of 18 dealers and research houses in Singapore and Malaysia on Monday forecast the ringgit to end the year at a median 3.37 to a dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar, typically deemed a safe-haven in times of crisis, fell to a 42-month low of 1.5740 to the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  "I see (dollar/Sing) buying from the local boys, the Americans, the inter-bank London parties and even Hong kong funds. Everyone is buying the dollar against the regionals," said a dealer with a foreign institution. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said selling was triggered in the morning out of Sydney on concerns over the extent of Singapore banks non-performing loans (NPLs). \par \par \uc2  Dealers said about S$30-S$40 million could have been sold in Sydney at around 1.5680, the previous year low, and stops were triggered all the way up to 1.5740. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said there could have been some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS), buying the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1.5750. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market expects the Singapore dollar to test 1.60 to the greenback within a week. \par \par \uc2  North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were not spared the Southeast Asian woes. Hong Kong dollar, South Korean won and Taiwan dollar sank in tandem. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar sank under selling pressure and was at 7.7475/85 to the greenback. Dealers said continued weakness on the blue chip Hang Seng stock index depressed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The won reached a historic low of 924.90 to the dollar, triggering two \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cushion its plunge. The won was spooked by fears of financial market turbulence following a chain of corporate defaults, bad debt and foreign investors' exodus, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is likely to rise to 930 this month and 940 in november or December. I cannot rule out the possibility of 950 by the end of this year," a foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar too tumbled against the greenback as investors grew nervous ahead of the summit meeting between China President Jiang Zemin and U.S. President Bill Clinton. The Taiwan dollar was at 30.530/630 to the dollar at 0430 GMT. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtal03wki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
