\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Drifts Lower Late In Quiet Market \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 1997\par 12:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is fractionally lower against the U.S. dollar in late Asian trading Thursday, compared with its level earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  But the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is stronger against the Malaysian ringgit, as the ringgit slipped against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  At 1000 GMT (6:00 a.m. EDT) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.5173, slightly higher than S$1.5170 in morning trading Thursday and up from S$1.5165 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Throughout Thursday the Singapore dollar has traded in a tight band against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the U.S. dollar ranging between a high of S$1.5185 and a low of S$1.5155, both of which were seen in early morning trading. \par \par \uc2  Trading was subdued Thursday, with most activity consisting of market participants buying the Singapore dollar against the ringgit, said traders. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is currently at S$0.5037, a touch lower from S$0.5041 earlier and below S$1.5165 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Speculation in the market centered on whether the Monatary Authority of Singapore, the island's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to maintain the ringgit/\b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar cross rate above S$0.5000. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said they had already seen signs of the MAS buying U.S. dollars against the Singapore dollar in order to force the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower against the ringgit. Others, however, scoffed at the idea, saying it was too far-fetched. \par \par \uc2  'That is not the MAS's style. They do not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the market is too volatile,' said a senior trader at a Singapore bank. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits has dropped to 2.625%-2.75% from 2.750%-2.875% earlier Thursday and late Wednesday. The three-month rate is flat at 4.0%-4.125%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-09-97 \par \par \uc2  1004GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9i06yoc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
