\par\par \b \uc2  REPEAT: =SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  At Record Lows As Baht Drops \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1997\par 15:35\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (Dow Jones)--Sweeping aside \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Thai baht plummeted by 7% against the U.S.\par dollar in onshore trading on Wednesday, ending Asian trading\par hours at a new all time low against the U.S. dollar.\par    The baht's plunge, precipitated by a credit rating\par downgrade and a debt default by Thailand's largest finance\par company, dragged other Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower. The\par Malaysian ringgit, the Indonesian rupiah and the Philippine\par peso also hit record lows against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as bank\par traders, investors and corporate treasurers all scrambled to\par sell regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The baht ended Asian trading at 37.85 baht to the U.S.\par dollar in the onshore market, down from 35.15 baht at\par Tuesday's close and nearly 32% below its level immediately\par before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's July 3 flotation. The Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par also fell to a record low in offshore trading, hitting 36.00\par baht to the U.S. dollar, down from 34.30 baht late the\par previous day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "There is no way one can be positive on Southeast Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at this stage. The other Southeast Asian\par countries are taking their cue from Thailand, and developing\par their own internal problems," said Vincent Low, a regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and fixed income strategist at Merrill Lynch\par International Bank in Singapore.\par    The latest slump in the baht came after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par broke through the key pyschological resistance level of\par 35.00 baht to the dollar late on Tuesday.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fall gained fresh momentum on Wednesday\par morning when U.S. rating agency S&P announced a\par long-expected downgrade of Thailand's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  debt\par rating from A to A-. The slide further accelerated on\par Wednesday afternoon when troubled Thai finance company\par Finance One said it would be unable to meet interest\par payments due on September 15.\par    With Thai corporations now in full flight to hedge their\par short term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -denominated debt - estimated by\par the bank of International Settlements to amount to $45.7\par billion - the interest to buy U.S. dollars was described by\par one trader at a Thai bank as "overwhelming".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  09-03-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0935EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt9301ukd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
