\par\par \b \uc2  =SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: Combined Stabilization Effort Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 1997\par 14:28\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The BIA's rumored action followed what was believed by\par traders to be \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the republic's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Large local\par banks were seen aggressively selling U.S. dollars, causing\par market participants to conclude a coordinated effort was\par under way to stabilize regional markets.\par    This view was bolstered when Goh Chok Tong, the prime\par minister of Singapore, made what were seen as reassuring\par market-friendly comments, while on an official visit to\par Japan.\par    "I take the view that you can't fight the market," he\par said.\par    "If the market believes that a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is overvalued,\par and they send it falling, it is difficult for central banks\par to fight it," he added, ruling out fixing exchange rates as\par a solution to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speculation.\par    Goh's statements were greeted positively by regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders and analysts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "Just making these statements is helping to prop up the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Chia Woon Khien, a treasury economist at\par Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken in Singapore.\par    Goh's remarks were seen in stark contrast to comments\par made earlier by Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad\par who threatened to strip brokers of their licenses to operate\par if they lent stock while promising to defend the Malaysian\par stock market "to our last sen."\par    "The authorities must recognize that markets have to be\par freely traded and acknowledge that there will be periods of\par volatility. Imposing new rules doesn't improve matters.\par Quite the opposite, it is seen as unprofessional and unfair\par to genuine investors and merely damps sentiment further,"\par said one regional strategist.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  08-29-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0828EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt8t01tx1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
