\par\par \b \uc2  S.E. Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  lose more flavour. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 740 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 1997\par 07:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 29 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost yet more flavour on Friday, with players piling into the U.S. dollar as stock markets crumbled across the region. \par \par \uc2  Rapidly dwindling investor confidence sent the Malaysian ringgit, Thai baht and Indonesian rupiah further into uncharted territory. The Singapore dollar hit a fresh 38-month low. \par \par \uc2  Weakness in the Philippine peso, Hong Kong dollar and South Korean won was muted by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the latest bout of selling was triggered by large U.S. hedge funds dumping the ringgit on growing fears of a trade deficit in July and investor panic after Kuala Lumpur's unexpected move to stop short-selling of major stocks. \par \par \uc2  But they said the malaise had spread as regional stock markets slumped, spurring dollar demand from companies, investors and portfolio managers. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit hit an early low of 2.9650 to the dollar against 2.8840/90 at the close of Asian trade on Thursday -- a drop of almost three percent in less than 24 hours. \par \par \uc2  "People are talking about all sorts of levels for the ringgit now. But I think the closest resistance (for the dollar) is at 3.00," a U.S. bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was at 2.9530/80 to the U.S. dollar at 0435 GMT. The Kuala Lumpur stock index fell to a low of 777.96 in morning trade, but staged a recovery to 811.17 at midday, 1.01 points below its previous close. \par \par \uc2  "There's a lot of panic building up and the market's overshooting now. I'm quite convinced that in one month's time, dollar/ringgit will be at 2.75, not at 3.00," a European bank dealer said. The ringgit last traded at 2.75 on August 21. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht, the trigger for the mayhem in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that began in May, was pulled to a new record low of 34.49 to the dollar onshore. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's become a regional factor right now. People lack confidence in the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the baht," a foreign bank dealer in Bangkok said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said volatility in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and continued economic and political uncertainty in Thailand spurred strong dollar demand from importers and foreign loan borrowers seeking to hedge their positions. \par \par \uc2  The baht was at 34.20/30 to the dollar onshore and at 34.15/30 offshore at 0435 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah remained below the key 3,000 level to the dollar all morning, hitting a low of 3,070 before tight domestic liquidity prompted a partial recovery. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rupiah rose to 80 percent and overnight swap was hovering around 18/19 points. The rupiah was at 3,005/15 at 0435 GMT against 2,930/35 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar bounced back from a low of 1.5375 to the U.S. dollar, sparking speculation of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There was no real reason for the U.S. dollar to go back down to 1.5250, so as usual the market will talk about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but we didn't see the usual \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  parties selling," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  She said buyers would snap up the U.S. dollar at 1.5250 and it could rise to 1.5550. It was at 1.5282/92 against 1.5175/85 at its Asian close on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso slipped to 30.365/415 to the dollar from its opening 30.30 and Thursday's 30.07 close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered dollars at the higher level of 30.45 pesos, suggesting tolerance for a weaker peso, but there was no sign of actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday when the peso fell to a record low of 30.45. It also raised bank liquidity reserves to siphon off funds that could be used for speculation. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won edged down to 901.90 against Thursday's 901.60 close, but dealers said trade was lacklustre, partly due to fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again after doing so repeatedly this week. \par \par \uc2  The normally stolid Hong Kong dollar slipped to a low of 7.7475/85 to the U.S. dollar while overnight interest rates shot up to 10 percent on spillover concerns. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8t00k7y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
