\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late Vs U.S. Dlr: Sharp Afternoon Reversal \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 1997\par 09:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar has continued to reverse losses of the past two days against its U.S. counterpart in volatile but illiquid afternoon trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  Profit-taking in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after at least two or three rounds of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which began in late morning trading, has triggered the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's turnaround, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore doesn't comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities but does have a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the currrency market to smooth out volatile movements in the Singapore dollar. Dealers said local banks, thought to be acting on behalf of the authority, sold U.S. dollars for Singapore dollars through the day. \par \par \uc2  'Position squaring' ahead of the weekend also helps explain the Singapore unit's revival, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar has tumbled to S$1.5005 around 0650 GMT (2:50 a.m. EDT), more than three Singapore cents down from S$1.5370, its intraday high touched around 0106 GMT and its highest level for 38 months against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at S$1.5185 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A mild recovery in the Malaysian ringgit against the U.S. dollar, as well as by other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which were all sold off in early dealings, has rubbed off on the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers added. \par \par \uc2  'Trading is very, very thin, another factor accounting for the 'Sing' dollar's recovery,' said a dealer at a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits has jumped to 7%-8% from 4.125%-4.25% in late Thursday trading. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank rate is slightly higher at 4.125%-4.325% from 4.0%-4.125% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0707GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8t06j2n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
