\par\par \b \uc2  Asian regionals stumble as Indonesian rupiah reels. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Phil Smith \par \uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1997\par 13:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 19 (Reuter) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had another traumatic day on Tuesday with the rupiah under severe pressure, serious enough to prompt a massive rise in interest rates by Bank Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's dive below 3,000 per dollar spurred the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into action and dragged other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. \par \par \uc2  Also under the gun was the Hong Kong dollar where forwards and short-term interest rates shot up amid a mounting belief that a full scale speculative attack on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the offing. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's problems began when the authorities last week decided to lift the old \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bands and allow it to float. With the bands in place onshore companies had felt relatively safe but now they find themselves underhedged. \par \par \uc2  "The locals have come on stream and it's a lot harder to contain locals than it is to contain the offshore players," said Chiang Yao Chye, Head of Asia Pacific Research at CIBC in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "The locals are hedging and in that sense it's real demand and therefore more difficult to deal with, speculators are just in there for a quick buck and they get out." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah regained some lost ground in late business after the rate hikes to 2,890.00 per dollar compared with its day's low of 3,030.00. \par \par \uc2  "So far all we saw were Jakarta names out there," a \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. There was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  It was this kind of seemingly unstoppable pressure which prompted the Indonesian authorities to say enough is enough and rates for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates (SBIs) were raised sharply. \par \par \uc2  One-week SIBs rose to 20 percent from 10.5, two-week to 22 percent from 11, one-month to 30 from 11.625 and three-months to 28 from 11.5. \par \par \uc2  "If the onshore guys are doing it, it is a cause for concern. You are then going against local demand some of this is obviously commercial in nature," said one analyst, noting that the same thing happened in Thailand when capital controls were first introduced local firms still wanted U.S. dollars so the pressure remained. \par \par \uc2  In Hong Kong, forwards remained firm and short-term rates hit 10 percent plus with the authorities pledging that speculators would be "burned" with high interest rates that would make it too expensive to launch a major attack on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The spot Hong Kong dollar ended firmer at 7.7385 after edging down to 7.7430. Most in the market do not expect a speculative attack to succeed given Hong Kong's access to substantial reserves and the political embarrassment of a devaluation so soon after the handover to China. \par \par \uc2  Also the competitive trade advantage that other Asian countries have got through allowing their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall does not apply to Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  It simply does not depend on exports as much as Southeast Asian countries. \par \par \uc2  "Hong Kong is more like a re-import and export hub for China. And most of its competitiveness is in the service industry. The strength of the Hong Kong dollar is not really a dominant factor," said a Singapore based U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Thai baht was still looking weak with the onshore rate down at 32.70 to the dollar compared with Monday's late level of 32.10. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it would lift the two-tier system "only at an appropriate time and when conditions in the money market are stable." \par \par \uc2  The market still suspects this will be sooner rather than later and has for a long time speculated that when the three month forward contracts put on in mid-May had matured the controls would be lifted. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit had a calmer day and managed to firm late in the session as the rupiah recovered after the rate hike. It was at a late 2.7870 per dollar against 2.7935 on Monday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8j00y5z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
