\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Higher Vs U.S. Dollar In Thin Early Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1997\par 04:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is slightly higher against the U.S. dollar in lackluster trading Tuesday morning as market participants await developments in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'There is some (U.S. dollar) selling interest from people looking to take profits at the current level, so it looks like we will see the market consolidating around here in the short term,' said a trader at a U.K. bank in Singapore, adding that the underlying trend was still to buy U.S. dollars for the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  At 0210 GMT (10:10 p.m. EDT Monday) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.5158, down from S$1.5170 in late Asian trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  In the absence of market-moving news affecting other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  the U.S. dollar is likely to fluctuate in a range of S$1.5080 to S$1.5200 In Tuesday's trading, said the U.K. bank trader. \par \par \uc2  If the U.S. dollar rises aharply against other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is could well test S$1.53 with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen as unlikely, he said. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit, meanwhile, is trading at S$0.5427 down from S$0.5439 late Monday, as the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  In the local money markets, short-term interest rates are up from levels seen Monday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits has risen to 4.375%-4.50% from 4.00%-4.25% late Monday. The rate was at 2.625%-2.75% late on Friday. The three-month interbank is unchanged from 3.875%-4.00% Monday afternoon, higher than 3.625%-3.75% late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0213GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8j062ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
