\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  off lows in London, more pain seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 15 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  got a brief respite in London trade on Friday after tumbling to new lows in the Far East but \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers predicted more turmoil next week. \par \par \uc2  The renewed slide in Asian units, triggered by Indonesia's decision to move to a managed float system for the rupiah, saw increased trade in the exotic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in London after another hectic session in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit pulled back to 2.7800/7850 against the dollar by 1500 GMT after tumbling on the local market earlier to 2.8210. \par \par \uc2  There was talk of fund profit-taking in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but dealers said they had seen no evidence of rumoured \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Bank Negara, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was also off its lows, pulling back to 1.5150/1.5170 after earlier breaching 1.52 while the Indonesian rupiah was sitting under 2,900 after hitting 2,940. \par \par \uc2  But the Hong Kong dollar was fragile, hovering around the key support level of 7.75 to the dollar which dealers said could well fall on Monday, a holiday in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  "The market seems to be targeting the Hong Kong dollar as the last peg left in Asia," said one dealer at an Australian bank in London. \par \par \uc2  Mitul Kotecha, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank, said markets were likely to remain rocky. \par \par \uc2  "We'll probably see more pressure next week. Fundamentals have gone out of the window so it's very difficult to judge at what level the market is going to let these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stop," he said. \par \par \uc2  Gregory Cronie, a trader at Indover Bank in Amsterdam, reiterated the view that the economic fundamentals for the rupiah remained strong and did not justify current weakness. \par \par \uc2  But he said there were concerns that Indonesian corporates with foreign loans had been caught short of dollars following this week's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunge, adding further uncertainty to the market mix. \par \par \uc2  -- Ben Hirschler, London newsroom +44 171 542 6414 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8f01atz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
