\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Ringgit hits weakest level since flotation. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Syed Azman \par \uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1997\par 09:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Aug 15 (Reuter) - The Malaysian ringgit took a fresh beating on Friday, hitting its lowest level against the U.S. dollar since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was officially floated in 1973, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Fresh speculative selling out of Singapore pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a record low of 2.8250 to a dollar, dealers said. It had recovered to 2.8000/50 by 0635 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the weakness in the Indonesian rupiah has spilled over to the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah dropped to a record low of 2,890 to the dollar on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Indonesia allowed it float the day before. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said thin market liquidity had made it easier to push the dollar/ringgit across the key psychological level of 2.8000. \par \par \uc2  "Most of the selling came out of Singapore. Volume is thin which makes it easy to move the market," said a dealer with a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "For now, it is likely that some players who were already long on the dollar may want to take some profits which may see the dollar/ringgit back to 2.8000 over the short term," said another \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer. \par \par \uc2  Talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Negara Malaysia at around 2.7910 earlier in the day could not be confirmed. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the worst may not be over as regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained under pressure. \par \par \uc2  "So long as the regional crisis is not over, weakness will remain," said a dealer with a Malaysian bank. "European players are likely to react when they enter later." \par \par \uc2  The ringgit, like the Thai baht, the Philippine peso and the rupiah, has been hit by speculative attacks over the past month. It has lost nearly 13 percent of its value. \par \par \uc2  Technically, the ringgit is seen heading for 2.8385 with support for the dollar seen at 2.7950, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -- Kuala Lumpur newsroom 603-201 4813; Fax-603-232 6752 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: kuala.lumpur.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8f016q2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
