\par\par \b \uc2  S.E. Asia  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  hit again after rupiah float. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1997\par 06:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 15 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah dropped to a new low on Friday after its effective float and brought other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  down with it. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah quickly lost an early firmness and fell to a record low of 2,890 to the dollar as overnight rates dropped back to 30 percent from an early high of 125 percent. \par \par \uc2  At 0430 GMT, the rupiah was at 2,875/80 at against its opening at 2,770/90. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates shot up due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tight short-term monetary policy and the maturity on Friday of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, when it sold about $500 million to defend the rupiah from a speculative onslaught. \par \par \uc2  "People are just toying around with the rupiah and it's affecting the other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well. We're looking for 3,000 on dollar/rupiah at some point," a Singapore-based dealer said. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, Bank Indonesia gave up its system of managing the exchange rate through the use of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  Analysts hailed the move as a welcome response to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and economic turmoil in the region, which has highlighted the need for greater exchange rate flexibility. \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund (IMF) welcomed the float, saying it would allow the Indonesian economy to continue a recent impressive performance. \par \par \uc2  "In present circumstances, a floating exchange rate will enhance the effectiveness of macroeconomic policies aimed at sustaining high rates of growth with financial stability," said acting IMF managing director Stanley Fischer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah's decline pushed the Singapore dollar to a 37-month low of 1.5220 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Nowadays, the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are traded as a group so if any one of them is being attacked, the rest of them will be pushed down as well," the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary authorities helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar recover from its lows, but dealers said it was still heading for 1.53. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fall also hit the Malaysian ringgit, which fell 2.7900/30 to the dollar against 2.7650/700 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the worst was not over for the ringgit given weak sentiment and the volatility in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They said the risk to the 2.80 level and beyond remained intact though the dollar was expected to face strong resistance at 2.7950. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht eased on continued commercial demand for the dollar, but activity was relatively muted as the market awaited an official announcement of a reported cabinet reshuffle, even though it was expected to have only a limited impact. \par \par \uc2  The baht was at 31.60/31.70 to the dollar in the domestic market against 31.50/31.60 late on Thursday. It was at 31.50/60 in offshore markets. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso fell to 29.71/81 to the dollar at 0430 GMT against its previous close at 29.49. \par \par \uc2  Manila traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to quote offer rates for the dollar at 10 centavos above the best market offer. The peso was expected to test a record low of 30, but dealers said some support was likely at 29.85. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar's decline was cushioned by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales of the U.S. dollar near T$28.727 in the face of persistent demand from importers. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was at T$28.726/727 against Thursday's T$28.725 close. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8f0136o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
