\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Stable Late After Earlier Fall On Rupiah Float \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1997\par 11:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is stable in afternoon trading Thursday, having slipped against the U.S. dollar earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  Mid-morning, the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped from around S$1.5000 to the U.S. dollar to an intraday low of S1.5150 on the news that the Indonesian rupiah would be floated. It later strengthened, however, and market participants say there is little interest in trading the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  'People are worried that the MAS will be in the market at S$1.5150,' said one trader at a U.S. bank here, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, the republic's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday an MAS official said that the Singapore dollar's exchange rate (then around S$1.4865) was appropriate, triggering a near 2% fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the belief that the MAS was reluctant to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Now with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar considerably weaker, there are heightened fears of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0900 GMT (5:00 a.m. EDT) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.5105, up a touch from S$1.5100 late morning and considerably higher than S$1.5055 aroundm 0000 GMT (8:00 p.m. EDT). \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is quoted at 1.625%-1.75%, lower than 1.875%-2.000% late Thursday morning. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank rate is steady at 3.6785%-3.8125%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0903GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8e061ff\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
