\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS -  \highlight22\uc2 Central bank \highlight\uc2  talks spur caution. \b0\par\par\uc2 762 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 1997\par 07:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 25 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were on slightly firmer footing on Friday morning as the market paused from its recent frantic selling to await the outcome of an Asian central bankers meeting in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  The one-day meeting, seen by some as the Asian G7, was expected to yield little more than warnings against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation and talk of cooperation, but dealers said sentiment had turned wary. \par \par \uc2  "The market is cautious in case anything happens. I would advise customers to trim down their positions or just square up," a European bank dealer in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some fears lingered about concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter the recent series of attacks on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but most were unconvinced, given the lack of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far. \par \par \uc2  "In general, it looks like the central banks have decided not to waste \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against market forces," a senior dealer at another European bank said. \par \par \uc2  "I'm a bit surprised they still think their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be that strong with the general U.S. dollar strength we've seen over the last 24 months," he added. \par \par \uc2  In Thailand, the baht remained weak on continued commercial dollar demand and worries about the financial sector. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said trade was calmer than in recent days and the baht had steered clear of the low of 32.70 to the dollar it hit on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Some Bangkok dealers said they saw strong support for the baht around the 32.30 level but they were not sure whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  "The market was quite calm this morning with only small buying. There was light commercial demand and the baht moved in a very tight band," a foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar bounced sharply back from its morning low of 1.4765 at the open, prompting talk of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS). \par \par \uc2  But most dealers attributed the move to nervous profit-taking by a market that had bought the U.S. dollar up aggressively in the last two days. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS wouldn't come in at this level, especially as the Finance Minister has said market forces should determine the exchange rate," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Richard Hu told parliament on Wednesday Singapore's exchange rate was determined by market demand and it would continue to be managed on a trade-weighted basis with a medium-term perspective. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was expected to trade a 1.4700-1.4760 range for the day. It was at 1.4729/39 at 0440 GMT. \par \par \uc2  In Malaysia, selling of the ringgit subsided but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upside was blocked around the 2.64 level to the dollar and dealers continued to predict more weakness. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think dollar/ringgit has seen a top yet. It should go to 2.70 eventually and the recent low of 2.6180/2.6200 should hold," a Singapore-based dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very quiet today, kind of in a squarish mode. They are probably waiting to see if any concrete measures emerge from Shanghai," said another Singapore dealer. \par \par \uc2  "The volume is extremely thin. 20-30 (million) dollars is moving dollar/ringgit by one big figure (100 points)," he added. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah remained depressed below the 2,600 level to the dollar but dealers said activity had slowed. \par \par \uc2  "It's still a regional factor. Fund managers who are playing in Jakarta have also exposures in Thailand and the ringgit. Once they move, all those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are affected," one said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,610/20 at 0440 GMT compared with an opening of 2,601/09. \par \par \uc2  In the Philippines, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars in the face of heavy commercial demand for the unit, helping to stem the peso's decline. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar calmed down, but tensions lingered after forwards shot up on Thursday, sparking fears of a speculative attack on Asia's most strongly pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  released Exchange Fund reserve figures after market close on Thursday, showing it held HK$569 billion at June 30, up 6.4 percent from December 31, 1996. \par \par \uc2  Analysts saw the move as aimed at scaring off speculators. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy in Kuala Lumpur (603-206 2323), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221 384-6364), Anchalee Koetsawang in Bangkok (662) 652-0642, Lilian Karunungan in Manila (632-841-8937), Sarah Davison in Hong Kong (852-2843-6441) and Sonali Desai in Singapore (65-8703090) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7p01xdh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
