\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Regionals on hold in late trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 1997\par 11:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 25 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets remained on hold in late trade on Friday as players awaited the outcome of an Asian central bankers meeting. \par \par \uc2  Most officials attending the one-day meeting in Shanghai declined to speak to reporters ahead of a news conference, scheduled for 0930 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The meeting was expected to yield little more than warnings against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation and talk of cooperation, but dealers said the market was taking nothing for granted. \par \par \uc2  "The market is cautious in case anything happens. I would advise customers to trim down their positions or just square up," a European bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were still some fears of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter the recent series of attacks on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but most were unconvinced. \par \par \uc2  "In general, it looks like the central banks have decided not to waste \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against market forces," a senior dealer at another European bank said. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) chief executive Joseph Yam told reporters in Shanghai he was not worried about speculators attacking the Hong Kong dollar, pegged at HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Fears of a speculative attack on Asia's most strongly defended peg were triggered on Thursday when forward rates shot up in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  But the market was calmer on Friday and the Hong Kong dollar traded in a range after the HKMA released figures showing it held HK$569 billion at end June, up 6.4 percent from end December, a move seen as aimed at scaring off speculators. \par \par \uc2  In Thailand, the baht recovered some ground after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Thailand deputy governor Chaiyawat Wibulswasdi said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall to 32 to the U.S. dollar was too low. \par \par \uc2  Chaiyawat also said he did not expect the baht to fall much further. \par \par \uc2  The baht was at 31.950/32.020 to the dollar at 0845 GMT onshore against 31.950/32.350 earlier. It was at 31.750/31.900 offshore. \par \par \uc2  Some Bangkok dealers said they saw strong support for the baht around the 32.30 level in the morning, but they were not sure whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar firmed through the 1.47 to the U.S. dollar level as London-based parties sold dollars. It was at 1.4675/85 to the U.S. dollar at 0845 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Its early recovery from a low of 1.4765 had spurred talk of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but most dealers attributed the move to nervous profit-taking after the U.S. dollar's spike up in last two days. \par \par \uc2  Selling of the Malaysian ringgit subsided but the market remained volatile and subject to sharp moves amid thin volumes and wide spreads. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the ringgit's recovery was blocked around the 2.64 level to the dollar and more weakness was likely in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think dollar/ringgit has seen a top yet. It should go to 2.70 eventually and the recent low of 2.6180/2.6200 should hold," a Singapore-based dealer said. The ringgit was at 2.6475/95 to the dollar at 0845 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah remained depressed below the 2,600 level to the dollar, but dealers said activity had slowed. \par \par \uc2  "It's still a regional factor. Fund managers who are playing in Jakarta have also exposures in Thailand and the ringgit. Once they move, all those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are affected," one said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,605/15 at 0845 GMT compared with an opening of 2,601/09. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso ended weaker in very light trade as banks sold dollars to commercial clients rather than the interbank market, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen capping the selling rate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars from 28.49 to 28.45 early in the day, but this was done on a selective basis, turning off many potential sellers. \par \par \uc2  The peso ended at 28.50 against 28.47 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy in Kuala Lumpur (603-206 2323), Mantik \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7p01x8u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
