\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore stocks a good buy as economy firms - DBS. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jacqueline Wong \par \uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 24 (Reuter) - Singapore equities are on the brink of recovery as the economic outlook improves in the second half of the year and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility recedes, DBS Investment Research director Mano Sabnani said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The stock market stands to capture more interest as recent sterling performers, such as property investments, stay depressed, he said. \par \par \uc2  "The market could recover about 25 percent for the next six to nine months starting in October," Sabnani told investors over lunch. Many stocks were trading at the lower end of their valuations, Sabani said. \par \par \uc2  He said the Straits Times Industrials Index (STII) would crawl out of its 1,900-2,100 trading band in the fourth quarter and could rise as high as 2,500 points. \par \par \uc2  The STII sank to its lowest level since 1995 in mid-July, dragged down by weak confidence in Asia and the flight of foreign funds on concerns over Thailand's economic woes and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But Sabnani said he based his sanguine outlook on the assumption that volatile regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were in the process of stabilising. \par \par \uc2  He said recent speculative attacks on the Singapore dollar were more a function of the lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  than poor fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's slide to a low of 1.47 against the U.S. dollar could in fact boost market sentiment as a softer \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would help exporters, he said. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's electronics sector, which makes up a hefty 70 percent of exports, should also enjoy better demand as U.S. orders for electronic components picks up and filters through. \par \par \uc2  Sabani said investors were likely to stay sidelined ahead of the corporate reporting season in September but the overall market should benefit from improved liquidity later. \par \par \uc2  The DBS report said some newly-listed stocks held promise, U.S. dollar stocks listed locally could gain from a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and electronic issues rise on the back of the sector's recovery. \par \par \uc2  And the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk of the Singapore dollar was limited, given a Singapore $115 billion foreign reserve and a current account surplus, Sabani said. \par \par \uc2  "We expect the fall of the Singapore dollar to stabilise around these levels," he said. \par \par \uc2  An economic recovery was also well underway and would gather steam into the second half of the year, he added. \par \par \uc2  A DBS Investment Research forecast gross domestic product (GDP) would steadily rise and see an average of 6.2 percent for 1997. \par \par \uc2  Sabnani said a lack of pressure on interest rates was also favourable to the stock market. \par \par \uc2  "The turnaround has begun. It began on July 17 when the market reached 1,920," he said. Now was the time to pick up good quality stocks which had fallen to attractive levels, he said. \par \par \uc2  DBS recommended buys on issues like automotive parts firm GPE Industries due to its investments in China, printed circuit board maker Gul Technologies because of major expansion plans and Hotel Properties, on its property earnings and foreign hotel prospects. \par \par \uc2  --Singapore newsroom (65 8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7o024g8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
