\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr/Early -2: Fin Min's Comments Trigger Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 1997\par 04:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  U.S. funds rushed in to sell the Singapore dollar after Richard Hu, Singapore's finance minister, said in Parliament Wednesday afternoon that the Singapore dollar's exchange rate is determined by market forces and that the recent weakness in the Thai baht and the Philippine peso 'should not pose a significant threat to (Singapore's) competitiveness.' \par \par \uc2  The market interpreted the remarks as an indication that the Singapore government wishes to see a weaker Singapore dollar, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent depreciation. \par \par \uc2  With the threat of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  believed diminished, the market has acquired significant momentum. Although the U.S. dollar has encountered some measure of upside resistance at S$1.4750, sentiment remains strongly bullish toward the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Many traders are targeting a level of S$1.48 to the dollar by the close of trading Thursday, and some see S$1.50 as a likely medium-term goal. \par \par \uc2  'Every one is buying U.S. dollars. U.S. funds and U.S. banks are leading the market, and the Singapore banks are following the trend,' said one trader at a U.S. commercial bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's fall Thursday morning comes as other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are sliding against a strong U.S. dollar. Against the ringgit, the U.S. dollar is trading at 2.6500 ringgit, up from 2.6390 ringgit in early trading. The U.S. dollar is also up sharply against the rupiah and the baht. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is at S$0.5566, up from S$0.5550 in late trading Wednesday as the Singapore dollar has plunged against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar money market rates are unaffected by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall. The overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is unchanged from late Wednesday at 4%-4.125%. Three-month interbank rates are also steady at 4.125%-4.375%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0234GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7o05dyn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
