\par\par \b \uc2  Shanghai central bankers meet seen as 'G7' of Asia. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Phil Smith \par \uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1997\par 05:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 23 (Reuter) - A meeting of Asian central bankers in Shanghai on Friday is being hailed as the region's 'G7'by \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in the wake of weeks of the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil. \par \par \uc2  In a still jittery market keen to hold U.S. dollars rather than regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the meeting could be something of a watershed given the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cooperation on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "This meeting will be like the G7 equivalent for this region," said Chiang Yao Chye, economist at CIBC Wood Gundy in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "The big issue for the market at the moment is this meeting in Shanghai as there is the possibility of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a statement that they are willing to join hands to support \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The meeting is being hosted by the People's Bank of China and the participants are due to arrive in Shanghai on Thursday evening. \par \par \uc2  Those attending include Japan, Hong Kong, Singapore, Malaysia, The Philippines, Thailand, Australia, New Zealand, South Korea, China and Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  It is a one-day meeting followed by a sight-seeing trip on Saturday before the bankers leave on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  However, sources in Shanghai say there are no plans to allow media access to the meeting and no briefing or communique is scheduled. \par \par \uc2  Regional central banks have helped each other out in the past. As the Thai crisis intensified in May, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to help shore up the sagging baht. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said Japan would keep in close contact with Asian economies such as Indonesia, Malaysia and Thailand to promote the stability of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the region. \par \par \uc2  Although Mitsuzuka said "that does not necessarily mean we are in a special cooperative alliance", statements such as this are enough to frighten the market given the huge \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves held by the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  "Although we've seen some big moves lately the actual selling behind them has been light and in some cases extremely light," said one Singapore-based trader. \par \par \uc2  "This meeting is certainly a golden opportunity for some major league jawboning from these guys about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cooperation. In markets this thin it will have an impact." \par \par \uc2  Traders said if there were anything forthcoming from the Friday meeting, it would most likely be after Asian market hours and give the market the whole weekend to digest any news. \par \par \uc2  But region \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could react to any news during European and U.S. time zones, they said. \par \par \uc2  The need for fresh regional cooperation on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was thrown into sharp relief on Tuesday when Malaysia reported an 8.8 billion ringgit, or 12.5 percent, fall in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to 61.9 billion in the first two weeks of July. \par \par \uc2  "This was a very nasty figure and just goes to show that in parts of the region there simply isn't the firepower to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there is another panic," said one Singapore based trader. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7n025ip\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
