\par\par \b \uc2  S.E Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  still on slippery ground. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1997\par 13:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 23 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained on slippery ground on Wednesday after coming under renewed pressure as the Thai baht slid to new lows. \par \par \uc2  Poor market liquidity and wide spreads added to market volatility as players turned increasingly nervous ahead of an Asian central bankers meeting in Shanghai on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said expectations the meeting might produce some form of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter the speculative onslaught on the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the dollar in demand. \par \par \uc2  "The big issue for the market at the moment is this meeting in Shanghai as there is the possibility of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a statement that they are willing to join hands to support \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Chiang Yao Chye, economist at CIBC Wood Gundy in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the baht's slide as it was pulled down by heavy commercial demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  "We noticed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the baht's fall at around the 32.50/32.60 to the dollar level," a senior dealer at a local bank in Bangkok said. \par \par \uc2  The baht hit a record low at one point with some dealers reporting transactions at as low as 32.60 to the dollar. At 1050 GMT, it was quoted at 32.250/32.550 onshore and 31.500/31.550 offshore. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the sharp plunge in the onshore market mainly to sales by importers seeking dollars to pay their bills and by corporations needing the dollar to repay foreign loans. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not need to sell large amounts of dollars to curb the fall because the pressure was mainly from local players trading in small amounts. \par \par \uc2  A senior Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official attributed the baht's weak tone to poor first-half earnings reported by local banks and finance companies. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar succumbed to fresh selling after comments by Finance Minister Richard Hu which players treated as yet another signal to buy the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Hu told parliament Singapore dollar's exchange rate was determined by market forces and its recent appreciation against its neighbours, especially the baht and Indonesian rupiah, did not pose a significant threat to its competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  "Our exchange rate policy should not be guided by short-term expediency considerations. We always focus on managing the exchange rate of the Singapore dollar on a trade-weighted basis with a medium-term perspective," Hu said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar fell to a low of around 1.4690 to the U.S. dollar after the comments, compared with 1.4645 earlier. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit was hit by fresh waves of selling by offshore U.S. banks despite talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars around 2.6350/70 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was quoted at 2.6355/85 to the dollar against a morning low of 2.6230. \par \par \uc2  "We are not sure if there is any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all. The said banks could be taking their own positions," a dealer at a Malaysian bank in Kuala Lumpur said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah remained weak after being dragged down by the slump in the baht. Spot rupiah was at 2,587/97 against an opening of 2,570/80. \par \par \uc2  "We saw some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the 2,580 level which helped boost the rupiah to 2,540 level in late morning, but uncertainty in Thailand kept the dollar tone biddish," a U.S. bank dealer in Jakarta said. \par \par \uc2  "If the rupiah could break the 2,500 resistance level, then there is potential for a strong comeback. But if it falls below the 2,600 level, speculators would launch an attack to test the band again," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso fell on commercial demand for dollars, closing at 28.50 to the dollar against 28.15 previously. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7n021pw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
