\par\par \b \uc2  Southeast Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  fragile despite lull. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 1997\par 11:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 22 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed signs of succumbing to renewed pressure in late Tuesday trade after making a brief recovery earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's surge to a 71-month high of 1.8071 marks in afternoon trade also weighed on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They said early gains in the Malaysian ringgit and Singapore dollar were driven by funds cashing in on the dollar's sharp rise, but did not reflect a change in sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "People who were long were just taking profit. I believe this regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness is not over yet," said a U.S. bank dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The market is awaiting the results of an Asian central bankers meeting in Shanghai later this week. \par \par \uc2  "This wave of contagion hitting the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be a relatively long running affair," said Desmond Supple, head of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at BZW Asia. \par \par \uc2  Supple said the central bankers meeting could yield strong verbal support for the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but added that he did not expect it to result in actual coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There's a broad-based reassessment of risk-reward valuations in the region. Given that genuine funds are leaving as well as speculators, that significantly increases the cost to the real economy of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah bounced back as offshore players triggered stop-loss dollar sales below the 2,600 level in afternoon trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at about 2,590 to the dollar at 0920 GMT after rising as high as 2,5670 against 2,600 around midday. \par \par \uc2  "We didn't hear of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today. The dollar was trading near the high of the band so people just got cautious," the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by one point to 2,378/2,682 after the rupiah became the latest victim of a speculative attack on Monday. It plunged about 150 points to a historic 2,665 low against the dollar before staging a marginal recovery on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the dollar was likely to encounter strong buying interest on any moves towards the 2,550 level. \par \par \uc2  In Malaysia, the ringgit slipped back a notch to 2.6230 to the dollar against 2.6200 earlier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a further drop towards 2.65 was likely despite expectations Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad would intensify his criticism of speculative attacks on the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  News reports quoted Mahathir, due to return to Malaysia on Tuesday after a two-month absence, as saying there may have been a political agenda behind recent attacks on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara Malaysia said its reserves had fallen to 61.9 billion ringgit as at July 15 against 70.7 billion a fortnight earlier, reflecting its recent efforts to defend the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar slipped back beyond the 1.46 level against the U.S. dollar in line with weakness in the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to head for 1.47/1.48 to the U.S. dollar despite positive export data and optimistic comments about the economy from government officials on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "In the short term, this is not so much about Sing dollar weakness as it is U.S. dollar strength," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht weakened, partly due to rumours that Thai opposition parties were planning to bring a no-confidence motion against the government, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "It's just natural for the opposition to create trouble with the current financial crisis in Thailand," said one. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso ended weaker at 28.15 to the dollar from 28 previously despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales of about $5.5 million during the day, Manila traders said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7m027z6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
