\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dollar surges as funds dump U.S. dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 10 (Reuter) - The Singapore dollar shot up in late afternoon trade on Thursday on stop-loss sales by funds that were long the U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Some stops were triggered below 1.4350. They could be very huge, especially by U.S. funds, which have been very long the U.S. dollar," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was quoted at 1.4295/305 to the U.S. unit at 0710 GMT against a morning low of 1.4367. \par \par \uc2  U.S. funds had been building long dollar/Sing positions since last week as anxieties about regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  spread following the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's shock move to a managed float of the baht. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's a healthy correction. I would buy the (dollar/Sing on) dips to see it back above 1.44," the dealer said, adding that dollar/Sing should remain supported around 1.4290/1.4300. \par \par \uc2  She said the Singapore dollar had been pushed up alongside a sharp rise in the ringgit as Malaysian interbank rates surged due to expectations of a liquidity squeeze. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/Sing has followed dollar/ringgit for the past few days. I think the Sing is being dragged by the ringgit move," she said, adding that the ringgit was pushed up by a sudden rise in the Kuala Lumpur overnight interbank rate. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was quoted at 2.4900/05 to the dollar at 0910 GMT after firming to 2.4875 against 2.5005/10 in the morning. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate rose to a high of 45/50 percent on sudden tightening of liquidity in the banking system as a result of Bank Negara's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday to support the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Although the actual size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not known, dealers said it could mop up anything between 2.5 billion and 5.0 billion ringgit from the system. \par \par \uc2  Settlement of Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  newsroom (65 8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7a02ucp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
