\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Falls Vs U.S. Dlr Early On Heavy Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1997\par 04:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is lower against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rose strongly against the Singapore dollar at the start of trading on a combination of U.S. fund buying and interbank technical trading, say bank traders in Singapore. By 0230 GMT (10:30 p.m. EDT), volumes of US$150 million to US$200 million had been traded, traders estimated. \par \par \uc2  Much of the buying interest came from a single U.S. fund which Monday failed to fully fill a large order to buy at S$1.4360 according to one trader at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The buying pressure pushed the U.S. dollar up to an early high of S$1.4385, leading traders to expect it to test the S$1.4400 level during the day. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  encountered selling interest and fell from its high, however, prompting traders to speculate that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, Singapore's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was selling U.S. dollars at the S$1.4385 level to smoothe exchange rate volatility. \par \par \uc2  'This looks like the MAS. They don't like sudden weaknesses, or sudden strengths,' said a trader at a leading Singapore bank. \par \par \uc2  The overall trend remains upward for the U.S. dollar against the Singapore dollar, traders say. The move has developed in part because investors are allocating assets away from South East Asia as a whole, and in part because traders are still concentrating on Singpore's relatively weak May trade figures, which showed a 1% fall in non-oil exports. \par \par \uc2  At 0245 GMT (10:30 p.m. EDT) the U.S. dollar is trading at S$1.4378, up from S$1.4366, its level in late trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is trading at S$0.5695, higher than S$0.5690 late Monday, but capped at S$0.5700 as long as the U.S. dollar is capped at 2.5250 ringgit by likely Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say traders. \par \par \uc2  In the local money markets, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar interest rates have dropped a touch at the short end of the curve, compared with their levels late Monday. The overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is at 2.375%-2.500%, down from 2.625%-2.750% late Monday. Three-month interbank rates are unchanged at 3.5%-3.625%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0258GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7804zhd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
