\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Sharply Higher Vs US Dlr On Ringgit Surge \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1997\par 12:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is up sharply from intraday lows against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in afternoon trading Tuesday, in reaction to the ringgit's surge against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit rocketed against the U.S. dollar in afternoon trading on what was widely identified in the market as aggressive dollar selling by Bank Negara Malaysia, Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At the same time, the Singapore dollar rose against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the ringgit dipped against the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  At 1000 GMT (6:00 a.m. EDT) the U.S dollar is trading at S$1.4365, well below its intraday high of S$1.4410, reached around 0730 GMT (3:30 a.m. EDT). Before it plunged, the U.S. dollar had risen steadily throughout Asian trading from levels around S$1.4370 in early trading. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the ringgit is quoted at S$0.5695, below its intraday high against the Singapore dollar around S$0.5710, touched at 0800 GMT (4:00 a.m. EDT). The ringgit remains above levels around S$0.5690 in early trading Tuesday, however. \par \par \uc2  Throughout the day speculators had been building up long U.S. dollar positions against the Singapore dollar, according to traders. \par \par \uc2  'The speculators were trying to push the U.S. dollar above resistance at S$1.4400, and were caught long by the ringgit's move. Now they are being forced to unwind,' said one trader at a major regional bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The violence of the afternoon's fall in the dollar led some traders to suspect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around S$1.4400 by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which they said sold dollars at the same time as Bank Negara was said to be selling. \par \par \uc2  The majority of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders dismiss the notion of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar's fall against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is simply a reaction to its move against the ringgit, asserted one trader at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Local money market rates have fallen since earlier Tuesday. The overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is at 2.00%-2.25%, down from 2.625%-2.750%, while three-month interbank rates are at 3.4375%-3.5625% from 3.50%-3.625%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1036GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7804z4a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
