\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. funds batter Singapore dollar - dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Angela Tan \par \uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 1997\par 14:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 3 (Reuter) - The Singapore dollar, traditionally a safe haven during Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, came under attack on Thursday from U.S. funds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It continued to slide in late afternoon trading as the U.S. funds tested its "safe-haven" status and interest rates in the city state fell. \par \par \uc2  By 1100 GMT, the Singapore dollar was trading around 1.4343/53 to the dollar compared to about 1.4300 on Wednesday. "The further weakness in the afternoon is basically because the Singapore interest rates came off," a dealer with a local bank told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's overnight interbank rate declined to around two percent on Thursday against 2-11/16 percent on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said U.S. funds continued to test how low Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could go against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Buying from various parties emerged after the Singapore dollar broke 1.4315/20 to the dollar and stop-losses were triggered. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. funds are still buying the dollar against the Sing. At this rate, I think we could see the Sing going to 1.4355 to the dollar soon," said another dealer with a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "People think the Singapore dollar won't be attacked because of its safe-haven reputation. But these U.S. funds are testing this reputation," a dealer with a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  "All the Americans want to do is to test the various stops to see how low the Sing dollar would go. They want to see how the weak shorts will be triggered out," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. dollar rose against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a British party emerged to buy on behalf of some U.S. funds from 1.4310 onwards. \par \par \uc2  "The Americans were buying the dollar against the Sing since late New York last night and they are just continuing to test all the stops," a dealer with a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  He said the first stop at 1.4320 was tested and triggered and now U.S. funds were looking to test the next resistance at 1.4355. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's "safe-haven" reputation was fairly vulnerable this time due to a weak stock market and an economy whose growth has slowed. \par \par \uc2  "Previously, the Singapore dollar, with the strong economy, was seen as a good buy every time something bad happens in the region. It's not so now. I would tend to be neutral on the Singapore dollar," said the dealer with the European bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , does \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the open market but it usually does not comment on its position. \par \par \uc2  MAS officials were not immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  In its annual report issued earlier this week, the MAS said it expected the Singapore dollar's modest rate of appreciation to continue. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt73031sx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
