\par\par \b \uc2  "Safe-haven" Singapore dollar gains on Baht float. \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 2 (Reuter) - The Singapore dollar saw some healthy buying against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday thanks to its status as a "safe-haven" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The move was in contrast to most of the other Southeast Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which were reeling from Thailand's move to float the baht, they said. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya shocked the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets earlier on Wednesday with an announcement that the country's exchange rate would be subject to a managed float, in which the baht's value would be set by market forces with immediate effect. \par \par \uc2  "We saw quite a bit of selling of the dollar against the Sing following news of the Baht float," a dealer with a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  "The Sing dollar is believed to be a safe-haven and whenever there is any uncertainty in the region, it will be the best bet," said a dealer with a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said activity on the dollar/Sing was "orderly" and not volatile like in some other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The dip in the dollar against the Sing was very fast and it quickly went back up to Tuesday's levels again," another dealer with a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  At 0755 GMT, the Singapore dollar was trading at 1.4296/06 to the dollar after hitting an early low of 1.4285 and a high of 1.4300. It was well-supported at 1.4285/90 to the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the open market by \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703083) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7202zwl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
