\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Tighter liquidity bolsters baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1997\par 06:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  * Thai baht strengthens as U.S. dollar weakens and amid tighter liquidity at home. Most dealers still reserving judgement on success of new finance minister \par \par \uc2  * Indonesian rupiah eases slightly but held steady by reports of dollar sell-orders just below current trading range \par \par \uc2  * Malaysian ringgit steady after overnight weakness amid rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar gains on U.S. dollar weakness and against ringgit sales \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 24 (Reuter) - The Thai baht firmed on Tuesday as the U.S. dollar weakened against the other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and amid tighter local liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading activity was thin as most dealers still prefered to stay on the sidelines to see how the new finance minister fared. \par \par \uc2  "People are still waiting to see what will happen next," said one Thai baht dealer in Singapore. "We don't expect a devaluation, but you never know." \par \par \uc2  Thanong Bidaya was appointed finance minister on Friday following the abrupt resignation of Amnuay Viravan after disagreements with political rivals. \par \par \uc2  In the offshore market, the baht was quoted at 24.800/25.100 to the dollar at 0400 GMT, compared with 24.900/25.100 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said the market remained quiet as most players appeared to square their positions ahead of the month-end. \par \par \uc2  In the domestic market, the baht firmed to 25.850/25.910 early against 25.950/26.050 late on Monday on the U.S. unit's weakness abroad and easing demand for the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar demand eased this morning. But some players still bought the dollar to cover positions ahead of the mid-year period," said one dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand set the mid-rate at 25.78 per dollar against 25.81 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah eased against the dollar in slow trading on Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was last quoted at 2431.00/32.00 at 0320 GMT against an opening of 2429.50/30.50. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar/rupiah appears capped at 2432 now as the market believes there are some heavy sell-orders at that level," said a dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He said the current bottom for dollar/rupiah was around 2429.50/2430.00. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 2,424/2,616 and its conversion band also at 2,424/2,472 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit fell against the dollar overnight amid rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank Negara in London. The ringgit fell again to below 2.5200 in Sydney but quickly recovered. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/ringgit was pushed up to 2.5215 in Sydney but came back down quickly," said a European bank dealer in Kuala Lumpur. "It triggered stop-loss dollar sales around 2.5190/00." \par \par \uc2  By 0400 GMT, the ringgit was quoted at 2.5170/80 a dollar. It closed at 2.5150/60 in Kuala Lumpur on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  again capped the dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the local dollar strenghtened through the morning to stand at 1.4267/77 at 0400 GMT after early trade at 1.4280 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  It also rose against the ringgit, with the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid at 0.5667 from 0.5673/5 in early trade. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman in Kuala Lumpur (603-206 2323), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221 384-6364), Anuchit Nguyen in Bangkok (662) 652-0642 and Chris Johnson in Singapore (65-8703199) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6o03ddq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
