\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore pledges to continue to defend Thai baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 19 (Reuter) - Finance Minister Richard Hu said on Thursday Singapore would continue to help Thailand defend its baht against speculators. \par \par \uc2  "We will continue with what we have been doing, which is to collaborate with the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but as you have seen so far the Thai authorities have managed quite a lot," Hu told reporters on the sidelines of a conference on project financing. \par \par \uc2  "I think there is no doubt that the present glitch (in Thailand) is a temporary one," he said following the resignation of Thai counterpart Amnuay Viravan. \par \par \uc2  On May 14, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly with the Bank of Thailand in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the baht against speculators. \par \par \uc2  MAS, effectively \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rarely admits \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  MAS deputy managing director Koh Beng Seng told reporters two days after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the move to defend the baht against speculators was effective. \par \par \uc2  But Amnuay's resignation on Thursday triggered another tumble of the baht in Asia, triggering a wave of hedging against other regionals, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said news that Thai Commerce Minister Narongchai Akrasanee also planned to resign would prompt more selling of baht. \par \par \uc2  The baht was pushed down to 26.300 against the dollar in late morning, but revived to 25.150/659 at midday. \par \par \uc2  Thai Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh said a new finance minister would be appointed on Friday but kept financial markets guessing as to who it might be. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6j03shx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
