\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Drifts Higher Late In Light Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 1997\par 11:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is marginally higher against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in afternoon trading Monday, compared to its late morning level. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar has drifted down throughout the day on light trading, in line with its decline against the yen to the current level of Y114.00 from Y114.85. \par \par \uc2  'The market believes that this is a good level to sell the U.S. dollar against the Singapore dollar,' said one trader at a U.S. bank in Singapore, reflecting the general view among traders. \par \par \uc2  Earlier sales of the U.S. dollar by Brunei-based funds helped push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down against the Singapore dollar, according to traders. That trend was later reinforced by London traders, who liquidated long U.S. dollar positions acquired the previous week when the dollar rose to over S$1.43 on the back of its climb to Y115.75 against the yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At 0920 GMT (5:20 a.m. EDT) the U.S. dollar is trading at S$1.4260, down from S$1.4287 at 0200 GMT (10:00 p.m. EDT Sunday). In the absence of large U.S. dollar moves against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar is likely to remain within a S$1.4200 to S$1.4300 range for the rest of the week, buoyed by commercial buying and possible \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  below S$1.4200, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is trading at S$0.5670, down from S$0.5679 in earlier trading. Activity in the cross rate is lacklustre, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In the local money markets, extreme short-term rates have fallen slightly. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is at 3.375%-3.500% from 3.500%-3.635% late morning. The three-month interbank rate is unchanged at 3.500%-3.625%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0940GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6g04dox\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
