\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Baht firms as BOT widens controls. \b0\par\par\uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1997\par 06:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 11 (Reuter) - The Thai baht firmed in offshore markets on Wednesday as the dollar hit lows not seen in almost seven months against the yen and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Thailand (BOT) tightened its grip on speculators, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at 23.850/23.900 to the dollar at 0440 GMT in the offshore market compared with 24.050/24.250 late on Tuesday. It was at 25.720/25.730 in the domestic market against 25.743/25.753 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The BOT set the mid-rate at 25.71 per dollar versus 25.72 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still very short of baht so there will be selling interest on any uptick in the dollar/baht," a European bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  She said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest move to cut off baht supply to foreigners through the stock market was also causing more selling of dollars for baht. \par \par \uc2  The BOT asked bank custodians on Tuesday not to accept transfers of borrowed and unpaid stocks sought by foreigners in a move to plug loopholes for foreigners to raise offshore baht. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said non-resident investors selling Thai stocks must be paid only in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the payment be made promptly to specific investors. \par \par \uc2  Signs that the capital controls imposed by Thai authorities since the baht came under speculative assault in mid-May were going to stay in place for some time yet fuelled jitters in the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Thai Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan said on Wednesday that current capital control measures introduced by the authorities to curb speculation in the baht were temporary, but more permanent ones would be announced soon. \par \par \uc2  A senior BOT official told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was working on measures to institutionalise the current controls to fend off future speculation, but did not provide a time frame. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, the rupiah showed a firmer bias amid tight money market liquidity but dealers said activity was confined to a narrow range. \par \par \uc2  "Trading is better than Tuesday but volume remains low. In fact the general view hasn't changed yet, with offshore slightly long in rupiah forwards," a Singapore bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,427.50/28.00 at 0440 GMT against an opening of 2,428.0/29.0. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trade was driven by relatively tight liquidity, keeping the dollar under pressure. Overnight money was traded at 13.0/14.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were mixed over the impact of the weakening dollar against the yen on dollar/rupiah rates. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. bank dealer said some seemed to attribute the rupiah's strength to the fall in dollar/yen but others were looking at the potential impact on Indonesia's budget, which would be negative if the yen continued to rise. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia has set a dollar/yen exchange rate of 110 for its 1997/98 budget starting April. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slipped to 110.97 yen in early Tokyo trade, its lowest level since November 20, 1996, on concerns about Japan's growing trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit recovered from its overnight lows as exporters sold the dollar near its highs. \par \par \uc2  "Exporters are selling the dollar around 2.5150 and this is capping the dollar/ringgit's rise," a European bank dealer in Kuala Lumpur said. \par \par \uc2  Strong dollar buying by two U.S. hedge funds at the 2.5100 level pushed the dollar/ringgit to a high of 2.5160 in thin overseas markets on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said many funds were still short dollars and were looking to cover their positions. \par \par \uc2  Across the border, the Singapore dollar's rise was thwarted by local bank buying of the U.S. dollar, raising fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/Sing will be under pressure but I think the local banks are around at the 1.4180 level. I would favour selling any rallies to 1.4220/30 or above to see an eventual test of the low end of 1.4100," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets through major local banks to stem sharp rises in the local dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman in Kuala Lumpur (603-206 2323), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221 384-6364), Anuchit Nguyen in Bangkok (662) 652-0642 and Sonali Desai in Singapore (65-8703090) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6b045g7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
