\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Flat As Funds Sell, Locals Buy \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1997\par 04:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is unchanged against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trading on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  At 0215 GMT (10:15 p.m. EDT Tuesday) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.4200, unchanged from levels Tuesday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  After dipping to a low of S$1.4193 in late trading, on what one trader at a Singapore bank described as 'massive stop losses going through', the U.S. dollar stabilized in the morning. \par \par \uc2  'The sellers are still out there. Funds are still getting out of their long dollar/Sing positions,' warns a trader at a leading U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Local corporations are still buyers at levels below S$1.4200, so if that level is breached the U.S. dollar is likely to fall no further than S$1.4180, he said. \par \par \uc2  'We are looking at a very tight range,' he says. \par \par \uc2  Also damping the possibility of further Singapore dollar appreciation are traders' and institutional investors' fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market should the U.S. dollar resume its fall. \par \par \uc2  The MAS was widely rumored to have bought U.S. dollars via local banks after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 100 point fall against the Singapore dollar on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Activity in the ringgit/Singapore dollar cross remains subdued, say traders. At 0215 the ringgit is quoted at S$0.5648, lower than S$0.5657 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money markets short-term rates are unchanged. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is steady at 2.625%-2.75%. The three-month interbank rate is 3.375% to 3.5% up from 3.3125%-3.4375% late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0230GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6b048mv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
