\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Closes Flat Vs U.S. Dlr In Heavy Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1997\par 11:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is flat against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in afternoon trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  After the U.S. dollar's 100 point fall to S$1.4180 in late trading Monday, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilised within a S$1.4200 to S$1.4210 range following rumors of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday morning. \par \par \uc2  Although the dollar has not moved outside that range since, volumes are considerable with European banks selling the U.S. dollar and local banks buying, according to one trader at a Singapore-based bank. \par \par \uc2  'The U.S. dollar is more likely to go down than up. There are a number of funds sniffing round looking to sell, but unless there is heavy selling from London, there is unlikely to be much further movement today,' said the head of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a major European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  If there is further heavy selling the U.S. dollar is likely to fall below S$1.4100, he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0900 GMT (5:00 a.m. EDT) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.4200, slightly lower than S$1.4207 at 0200 GMT Tuesday (10:00 p.m. EDT) and well below S$1.4269 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  In light trading the ringgit is quoted at S$0.5657, slightly lower than S$0.5663 earlier, and down from S$0.5682 Monday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money markets short-term rates are steady, having fallen over recent days. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is unchanged from Tuesday morning at 2.625-2.75%. The three-month interbank rate is 3.3125%-3.4375%, also unchanged. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0917GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6a048us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
