\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Up Vs U.S. Dollar Late, But Off Highs \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1997\par 11:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is higher against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late-afternoon trading Monday, in line with the U.S. dollar's earlier fall against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar traded to a low of S$1.4265 in late-morning activity, encountering strong buying at that level, according to traders. \par \par \uc2  Some traders suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore had stepped in to halt the Singapore dollar's rise, saying that Singapore banks were the biggest buyers. \par \par \uc2  One head trader at a \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank played down the notion of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however. \par \par \uc2  'While it is possible the MAS came in to mop up some excess liquidity, it was not buying aggressivly. If the U.S. dollar is heading down to levels around Y110, the MAS will really not be too concerned if dollar/Sing is at S$1.42,' he said. The U.S. dollar fell to a six-month low of Y111.90 during Monday trading. \par \par \uc2  Other traders also dismissed the idea that the MAS was active. \par \par \uc2  'The market is very bid at S$1.4265 with corporates buying. A lot of people were caught short and rushed to cover,' said one trader at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0845 GMT (4:45 a.m. EDT) the market has stabilised with the U.S. dollar trading at S$1.4269, down marginally from S$1.4271 at 0200 GMT and still well below S$1.4308 in late trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is quoted at S$0.5682, a touch lower than S$0.5683 in earlier trading and below S$0.5687 late Friday. Traders described activity in the cross rate as near non-existent. \par \par \uc2  In the local money markets, interst rates have resumed their recent downward trend. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is at 2.875%-3.00% down from 3.00%-3.125% in late morning. The three-month interbank rate is at 3.4375%-3.5625% down from 3.50%-3.625% earlier. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0902GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt69047lc\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Singapore near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\br